# Assumptions narrow inputs; C code runs through the C frontend.
# A clamp whose low bound can never be reached under the assumption.
simplify x in [0, 100] nofile
```spv
%a = OpExtInst %uint %glsl UClamp %x %uint_200 %uint_255
OpStore %out %a
```
# A compare that is constant under the assumption.
simplify x in [0, 4] nofile
```spv
%c = OpULessThan %bool %x %uint_8
%k = OpSelect %uint %c %x %uint_8
OpStore %out %k
```
# C input: multiply/remainder by constants.
SAT simplify nofile
```c
unsigned f(unsigned x){ return (x * 8u) / 4u + (x & 255u) % 256u; }
```
# C input with an assumption on a shift amount.
SAT simplify n in [1, 31] nofile
```c
unsigned shr(unsigned x, unsigned n){ return (x << n) >> n; }
```
